# Constants And Environment Rules

Centralize runtime configuration.

## Requirements
- `src/config/env.js` must be the only place that reads raw environment variables.
- All required environment variables must be validated at startup.
- Secret values must not have silent fallbacks.
- Non-secret runtime constants must live in config modules, not scattered literals.
- Environment variable names use `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`.
- Feature flags and provider selection must be config-driven.
